  "character_tex": "Parafermion characters (string functions) $\\Phi^l_m$ from $\\chi^{SU(2)_k}_l(\\tau,z) = \\sum_{m\\in\\mathbb{Z}_{2k}}\\Phi^l_m(\\tau)\\,\\Theta_{m,k}(\\tau,z)/\\eta(\\tau)$, fields $(l,m)\\sim(k-l,m+k)$. On the $C$-fixed fields $(l,0)$, $l$ even, the twined characters are $t_l = (-1)^{l/2}\\eta(2\\tau)^{-1}\\sum_{x\\equiv l+1\\ (2K)}\\sin\\frac{\\pi x}{2}\\,q^{x^2/4K}$, $K = k+2$, and $\\Phi^{l,\\pm}_0 = \\frac12(\\Phi^l_0\\pm t_l)$. Twisted characters: $\\mathcal{T}_y = \\eta(\\tau/2)^{-1}\\sum_{n\\in\\mathbb{Z}}(-1)^n q^{(y+2Kn)^2/16K}$ ($y\\equiv k$ mod 2, $0<y\\le k$), of weight $h = \\frac{k-2+y^2}{16K}$; $\\mathcal{T}^{\\pm}_y$ are its parts with $L_0-h$ in $\\mathbb{Z}$ and $\\mathbb{Z}+\\frac12$. Here $k = 7$.",
  "description": "Orbifold of the diagonal $\\mathbb{Z}_{7}$ parafermion theory by charge conjugation $C: \\Phi^l_m\\to\\Phi^l_{-m}$ (Dijkgraaf-Vafa-Verlinde-Verlinde 1989). The untwisted sector keeps one copy of each pair $\\{(l,m),(l,-m)\\}$ and the $C$-even parts of the 4 fixed fields $(l,0)$; the twisted sector $Z_{C,1} = \\sum_y|\\mathcal{T}_y|^2$ is the Poisson resummation of $Z_{1,C} = \\sum_l |t_l|^2$, projected to integer spin. Lightest twisted state: $h = \\bar h = 1/24$.",
